# Complexity Analysis - Smart Campus Resource Management System

## 1. Linear Search ($O(n)$)
- Traverses through the vector sequentially. Worst case checks every element, resulting in $O(n)$ time complexity.

## 2. Bubble Sort ($O(n^2)$)
- Uses nested loops to compare adjacent student IDs. Yields a quadratic time complexity of $O(n^2)$.

## 3. 2D Array Matrix Processing ($O(n^2)$)
- Processes a static 2D array using nested loops for department resource allocation.
